1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,387
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,512 --> 00:00:54,346
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,472 --> 00:00:55,306
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:02:18,430 --> 00:02:19,932
You can give it back now.

6
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,608
I can read the room.

7
00:02:30,401 --> 00:02:32,653
I won't go back to him. Give it back.

8
00:02:39,785 --> 00:02:41,120
Break up with Namgung Ho.

9
00:02:43,247 --> 00:02:44,748
We have no chance anyway.

10
00:02:45,624 --> 00:02:47,585
If you can read the room, you should know.

11
00:02:48,127 --> 00:02:51,213
There's no room for us between them.

12
00:02:53,632 --> 00:02:56,176
-So--
-You really do love Lee Mi-do.

13
00:02:59,138 --> 00:03:00,973
I thought you weren't serious then.

14
00:03:02,474 --> 00:03:03,934
I thought you were crazy.

15
00:03:06,979 --> 00:03:08,355
Let's form an alliance.

16
00:03:10,649 --> 00:03:13,485
You like Namgung Ho,
and I like Lee Mi-do.

17
00:03:14,153 --> 00:03:15,654
But we only have one month.

18
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:17,823
How about a strategic approach?

19
00:03:18,157 --> 00:03:18,991
A FEW DAYS AGO

20
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:20,492
What's the plan, exactly?

21
00:03:23,454 --> 00:03:25,080
Here's what I was thinking.

22
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:28,417
Go on an overnight business trip,
no matter what.

23
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:31,378
Nothing even has to happen.

24
00:03:31,503 --> 00:03:33,339
Just go.

25
00:03:34,798 --> 00:03:37,509
Just knowing it happened
would make someone anxious,

26
00:03:37,635 --> 00:03:38,636
angry,

27
00:03:40,054 --> 00:03:41,055
and suspicious.

28
00:03:42,890 --> 00:03:46,936
All we need is a tiny spark
to break their trust.

29
00:03:48,187 --> 00:03:49,188
That's all.

30
00:03:49,313 --> 00:03:50,272
I refuse.

31
00:03:53,317 --> 00:03:55,861
I guess you aren't serious
about Namgung Ho.

32
00:03:57,446 --> 00:04:01,825
People would do worse things
if they're in love with someone.

33
00:04:01,951 --> 00:04:03,994
Gladly and gratefully.

34
00:04:06,121 --> 00:04:07,289
That's what one does.

35
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:10,042
You're the one who isn't serious.

36
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:11,627
Give me a break.

37
00:04:11,752 --> 00:04:15,673
I hate you, and you disgust me.

38
00:04:17,925 --> 00:04:20,260
Because the person I love
suffered because of you.

39
00:04:20,928 --> 00:04:22,179
And because of you,

40
00:04:22,888 --> 00:04:24,515
he's hurting even at this very moment.

41
00:04:26,558 --> 00:04:27,643
I'm begging you.

42
00:04:29,311 --> 00:04:30,688
Break up with Ms. Lee.

43
00:04:32,106 --> 00:04:33,357
Stop messing

44
00:04:34,316 --> 00:04:35,651
with Ms. Lee.

45
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:42,658
Yeah, fair enough.
I get how you felt back then.

46
00:04:43,409 --> 00:04:45,160
So I'm breaking up with her.

47
00:04:46,537 --> 00:04:50,249
But it seems you've had a change of heart.

48
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:57,214
Stop it.

49
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:00,884
You're only making it harder
on Namgung Ho.

50
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:01,844
Don't you know?

51
00:05:01,969 --> 00:05:02,970
I know.

52
00:05:04,972 --> 00:05:06,056
But…

53
00:05:07,474 --> 00:05:10,019
Namgung Ho shouldn't suffer
because of you.

54
00:05:10,936 --> 00:05:13,063
And I hate seeing him hurt over Ms. Lee.

55
00:05:14,356 --> 00:05:15,691
Originally,

56
00:05:16,442 --> 00:05:17,484
really, at first,

57
00:05:18,402 --> 00:05:20,738
my goal was to make him happy
for one month.

58
00:05:22,197 --> 00:05:23,991
But that's changed.

59
00:05:25,576 --> 00:05:27,578
I want to make him happy forever.

60
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:30,205
I want…

61
00:05:31,623 --> 00:05:33,792
to make him overwhelmingly happy forever.

62
00:06:02,071 --> 00:06:03,363
Namgung.

63
00:06:05,157 --> 00:06:06,366
Namgung, look at me.

64
00:06:09,411 --> 00:06:10,537
Look at me.

65
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:34,520
You must know

66
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:38,273
how miserable and hurt I feel.

67
00:06:39,108 --> 00:06:40,442
But, Namgung,

68
00:06:42,319 --> 00:06:43,445
I know.

69
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:49,118
How sorry you are.

70
00:06:51,286 --> 00:06:53,455
How angry you are at yourself,

71
00:06:55,207 --> 00:06:56,750
how you hate all this,

72
00:06:57,626 --> 00:06:59,128
and how much pain you're in.

73
00:07:01,922 --> 00:07:03,298
I know that too.

74
00:07:05,592 --> 00:07:07,261
I know all too well.

75
00:07:16,937 --> 00:07:18,105
It's my fault.

76
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,526
I brought it all on myself,

77
00:07:23,944 --> 00:07:25,821
and I'm the one to blame.

78
00:07:29,199 --> 00:07:33,996
I was so arrogant and vile
that I caused all this.

79
00:07:35,164 --> 00:07:36,915
You did nothing wrong.

80
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:40,043
It's all my fault.

81
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:43,422
Lee Mi-do, that's not fair.

82
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:46,592
-If you do this, I--
-Namgung.

83
00:07:48,594 --> 00:07:50,804
I guess I finally grew up.

84
00:08:06,695 --> 00:08:08,322
Let's see this through.

85
00:08:10,741 --> 00:08:12,326
Let's take it

86
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:14,786
all the way to the end.

87
00:08:16,788 --> 00:08:18,457
Our month is almost up.

88
00:08:19,458 --> 00:08:21,084
So let's do it

89
00:08:21,210 --> 00:08:22,669
with no regrets,

90
00:08:24,046 --> 00:08:25,589
all the way to the end.

91
00:08:29,593 --> 00:08:30,427
Okay?

92
00:08:55,953 --> 00:09:01,833
13. WHO WILL WE BE WITH IN TEN YEARS?

93
00:09:15,305 --> 00:09:17,933
THE SECRETS OF SCREENPLAY STRUCTURE

94
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:27,192
Is our homeroom teacher insane?

95
00:09:27,317 --> 00:09:29,319
Twenty laps in this weather.

96
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:33,824
It was you, right?

97
00:09:34,449 --> 00:09:36,660
You're the one who keyed their car.

98
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,037
Since they gave you a zero.

99
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:46,295
Namgung Ho's loyalty is unmatched.

100
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:23,332
What are you doing?

101
00:10:24,499 --> 00:10:26,501
Where's volume nine? No volume nine?

102
00:10:50,192 --> 00:10:51,902
It was the homeroom teacher's fault.

103
00:10:53,070 --> 00:10:55,405
They lost my assignment
and gave me a zero.

104
00:10:58,492 --> 00:11:00,827
Are you an idiot? Why raise your hand?

105
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:03,538
Did you think I'd thank you?

106
00:11:05,332 --> 00:11:07,209
Why would you run 20 laps?

107
00:11:07,334 --> 00:11:11,213
Remember when Lee Yeong-do
almost burned down that rib joint,

108
00:11:11,338 --> 00:11:13,799
and you cleaned it for a month?
I know everything.

109
00:11:15,801 --> 00:11:17,761
You paid for Wan-do's swim lessons

110
00:11:17,886 --> 00:11:19,513
and bought his swimsuit too, right?

111
00:11:21,598 --> 00:11:23,100
Stop living like that.

112
00:11:23,225 --> 00:11:25,018
People will walk all over you.

113
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:26,937
Seriously, why live like that?

114
00:11:31,316 --> 00:11:32,401
You really don't know?

115
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:37,406
You really have no idea why I did that?

116
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:39,533
That's right.

117
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:42,160
I have no idea.

118
00:11:42,994 --> 00:11:44,871
Then just stay clueless.

119
00:11:46,957 --> 00:11:49,584
Fine! I'll keep living like this.

120
00:11:49,709 --> 00:11:51,336
I'll stay immature my whole life!

121
00:11:53,296 --> 00:11:55,924
I'll never be an idiot
or a pushover like you!

122
00:12:24,661 --> 00:12:26,872
Park Su-a, for breach of trade secrets,

123
00:12:26,997 --> 00:12:29,749
code of ethics violations,
and suspected bribery,

124
00:12:29,875 --> 00:12:33,462
is suspended pending the inquiry,
but will report to work as normal.

125
00:12:47,225 --> 00:12:49,978
They want you to type this up.

126
00:12:50,103 --> 00:12:52,314
The sensory evaluation sheets?

127
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:56,151
Why bother when an OCR scan can do it?

128
00:12:56,276 --> 00:12:59,321
Would you rather organize receipts?

129
00:13:05,952 --> 00:13:08,038
TF Team 3 will be disbanded soon.

130
00:13:09,039 --> 00:13:10,749
I'm sorry I can't help.

131
00:13:16,922 --> 00:13:18,423
Don't talk to me.

132
00:13:19,341 --> 00:13:20,717
Don't look.

133
00:13:22,177 --> 00:13:26,681
Our coup failed,
so now it's every man for himself.

134
00:13:29,392 --> 00:13:31,520
I'll only take the blame for the disposal.

135
00:13:32,604 --> 00:13:35,815
What you did, you did on your own.

136
00:13:36,942 --> 00:13:38,860
It has nothing to do with me.

137
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,593
SCRAP PAPER BIN

138
00:14:08,431 --> 00:14:09,558
Take them back out.

139
00:14:10,559 --> 00:14:12,143
Take them out and put them back.

140
00:14:13,979 --> 00:14:14,813
No, I won't.

141
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:25,115
You know Jeong and Seok went to Thailand?

142
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:28,034
They're on vacation,
not suspended at home.

143
00:14:28,159 --> 00:14:30,245
-Executive Director Yoon, too.
-So what?

144
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:33,540
You can take time off
and go to Thailand too.

145
00:14:33,665 --> 00:14:36,042
You're not penalized yet,
so you can take time off.

146
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:39,004
-You have plenty of days left.
-That's not what I'm talking about…

147
00:14:43,341 --> 00:14:45,010
People will be back soon.

148
00:14:45,135 --> 00:14:46,720
If people see you with me--

149
00:14:46,845 --> 00:14:47,929
Finish typing.

150
00:14:48,763 --> 00:14:50,849
Or I'll stay right next to you.

151
00:14:50,974 --> 00:14:52,100
Assistant Manager Namgung.

152
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:54,019
Lunch is almost over.

153
00:14:54,144 --> 00:14:55,353
People are coming.

154
00:14:56,146 --> 00:14:58,106
Want to make things hard for me?

155
00:15:27,844 --> 00:15:31,014
It's not CGI.
I shot 52 seconds a day for four days.

156
00:15:31,139 --> 00:15:33,224
-You're sure it's not CGI?
-It's not.

157
00:15:33,350 --> 00:15:35,727
If I check and you're lying, you're dead.

158
00:15:36,895 --> 00:15:40,148
No studio would let you shoot
a sunset for four days.

159
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:41,650
Of course I'm lying.

160
00:15:42,484 --> 00:15:43,318
You're crazy.

161
00:15:43,443 --> 00:15:47,113
I wrote lines and shot scenes,
then cut everything and kept the sunset!

162
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,491
Admit it, I'm cool, right?

163
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:51,159
You're so annoying.

164
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:53,286
I can't argue with that.

165
00:15:53,411 --> 00:15:55,705
-Cool, right?
-Yeah, a little.

166
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:00,418
What about the ending scene
with that moth on the window?

167
00:16:00,543 --> 00:16:01,920
-Lee Mi-do.
-Yeah?

168
00:16:02,045 --> 00:16:03,797
-I'll only tell you.
-Okay.

169
00:16:04,839 --> 00:16:06,925
I only saw it in the rough cut.

170
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:08,677
Really?

171
00:16:08,802 --> 00:16:10,762
The editor added it for impact.

172
00:16:10,887 --> 00:16:12,555
Wow, that's crazy.

173
00:16:12,681 --> 00:16:14,432
How'd you shoot the airport scene?

174
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:16,685
For that, I got
the drone and lighting teams

175
00:16:16,810 --> 00:16:18,937
-and I--
-Do you own this place?

176
00:16:21,856 --> 00:16:23,233
Quiet down.

177
00:16:25,568 --> 00:16:27,320
My partner ghosted me,

178
00:16:27,445 --> 00:16:29,989
so I'm in a terrible mood.

179
00:16:32,659 --> 00:16:33,493
Quiet, please.

180
00:16:33,618 --> 00:16:35,578
We're sorry.

181
00:16:42,877 --> 00:16:43,753
Hey.

182
00:16:44,629 --> 00:16:46,464
Since he said "partner,"

183
00:16:47,382 --> 00:16:49,801
I think he swings my way.

184
00:16:51,553 --> 00:16:54,472
Was that flirting?
He kept staring at me earlier.

185
00:16:54,597 --> 00:16:55,765
Hey.

186
00:16:55,890 --> 00:16:58,560
If you're going to wear knockoffs,
get high-quality ones.

187
00:16:59,269 --> 00:17:03,982
Once you get paid, just go to the store
and buy the real thing.

188
00:17:04,107 --> 00:17:05,316
Chin up.

189
00:17:05,859 --> 00:17:06,776
Good.

190
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:11,030
-Is it that obvious?
-Yeah, totally.

191
00:17:15,869 --> 00:17:16,745
He's handsome.

192
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:18,538
Seriously, what is with you?

193
00:17:24,794 --> 00:17:26,421
Ms. Lee, don't overdo it.

194
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:30,675
You're already a mess
over Namgung Ho and Park Su-a.

195
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,344
Don't push yourself.

196
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:36,139
Are you in any position
to celebrate others?

197
00:17:36,264 --> 00:17:39,017
Why? Does it look like I'm pushing myself?

198
00:17:39,142 --> 00:17:40,185
Aren't you?

199
00:17:40,310 --> 00:17:42,395
No, I'm not.

200
00:17:49,778 --> 00:17:53,615
Mi-do, where did I leave off?

201
00:17:54,324 --> 00:17:55,200
Right!

202
00:17:56,451 --> 00:17:58,286
The fall from the building.

203
00:17:58,411 --> 00:18:00,038
-That was--
-Tak Jackson.

204
00:18:00,705 --> 00:18:01,539
Yes?

205
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:03,792
Remember back then?

206
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:10,340
Three years ago, when Park Jae-yeong's
casting fell through,

207
00:18:10,465 --> 00:18:13,259
the studio told you to give up.

208
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:15,011
Remember what you said?

209
00:18:16,554 --> 00:18:18,306
Oh, yeah!

210
00:18:19,474 --> 00:18:22,477
That we'd quit movies
and start a YouTube channel.

211
00:18:22,602 --> 00:18:25,605
Masked Mouse, trashing the film industry!

212
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:28,525
Right, we said we'd do that!

213
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:37,242
-No?
-"I want to write this story."

214
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,204
"I really want to make this."

215
00:18:43,623 --> 00:18:45,625
"I have to make this."

216
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:48,294
You said that. Don't you remember?

217
00:18:48,962 --> 00:18:50,213
I knew right then.

218
00:18:53,216 --> 00:18:54,968
I thought, "This movie will get made."

219
00:18:56,553 --> 00:18:58,388
"This bastard's going to make it."

220
00:18:59,848 --> 00:19:03,810
"This is what a real director looks like."

221
00:19:05,186 --> 00:19:08,356
"It's someone like him
who should be making movies."

222
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:20,577
People calling your movie
a  Lord of the Rings  knockoff?

223
00:19:20,702 --> 00:19:22,328
Screw them.

224
00:19:22,453 --> 00:19:25,999
Don't listen to them saying
you had no real competition.

225
00:19:26,124 --> 00:19:29,043
Tell them to cut the bullshit
about getting lucky.

226
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:30,670
It wasn't just the cast.

227
00:19:30,795 --> 00:19:32,589
It wasn't.

228
00:19:32,714 --> 00:19:34,340
Listen to me.

229
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:37,760
It worked out

230
00:19:38,970 --> 00:19:40,471
because you did a great job.

231
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:44,058
And because you didn't quit,

232
00:19:45,059 --> 00:19:48,229
you made it happen.

233
00:19:50,398 --> 00:19:51,691
Right?

234
00:19:59,532 --> 00:20:00,992
Luc Mi-do.

235
00:20:01,117 --> 00:20:04,412
A really good runner

236
00:20:05,538 --> 00:20:09,167
only sprints in the last two kilometers.

237
00:20:09,792 --> 00:20:11,336
Yeah.

238
00:20:11,461 --> 00:20:15,214
But you're not at the last 2K yet.

239
00:20:16,299 --> 00:20:18,343
That's why it's so tough.

240
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:20,511
Hang in there, okay?

241
00:20:20,637 --> 00:20:23,348
Seriously? You call that comforting?

242
00:20:26,726 --> 00:20:29,562
Sorry, that was a bad example.

243
00:20:29,687 --> 00:20:31,189
You think so?

244
00:20:34,901 --> 00:20:37,445
Hey!

245
00:20:53,336 --> 00:20:54,337
Luc Mi-do!

246
00:21:05,306 --> 00:21:06,474
Can I buy you dinner?

247
00:21:13,106 --> 00:21:15,483
At times like this, you need to eat well.

248
00:21:15,608 --> 00:21:17,986
Food is 80% of what keeps you going.

249
00:21:20,905 --> 00:21:21,906
Su-a.

250
00:21:24,784 --> 00:21:26,119
Sweetheart.

251
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,288
Deok-sun.

252
00:21:32,083 --> 00:21:33,584
Can I buy you dinner?

253
00:21:34,627 --> 00:21:36,754
Let's get something good to eat.

254
00:21:38,881 --> 00:21:40,133
Please tell me…

255
00:21:42,468 --> 00:21:44,053
the secret Ms. Lee doesn't know.

256
00:21:44,178 --> 00:21:46,514
You said you'd tell me
after 10 seconds of eye contact.

257
00:21:50,101 --> 00:21:51,352
I know it's childish.

258
00:21:51,477 --> 00:21:52,770
I hate being like this.

259
00:21:52,895 --> 00:21:55,898
-But--
-The reason I've never told Lee Mi-do

260
00:21:57,108 --> 00:21:59,277
is because I love her so much.

261
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:03,448
It's truly humiliating for me.

262
00:22:06,075 --> 00:22:08,286
So I never wanted her to find out.

263
00:22:08,411 --> 00:22:09,245
And…

264
00:22:11,372 --> 00:22:13,332
I can't tell you for the same reason.

265
00:22:19,130 --> 00:22:20,298
You're a coward.

266
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:24,343
You're being really, really cowardly.

267
00:22:24,469 --> 00:22:25,344
I know.

268
00:22:26,137 --> 00:22:27,805
So I'm buying you a good meal.

269
00:22:28,556 --> 00:22:29,515
What do you want?

270
00:22:32,018 --> 00:22:33,186
No, thank you.

271
00:22:34,312 --> 00:22:35,772
I'm going to cook for you.

272
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,650
I'll make you
something really, really good.

273
00:22:42,403 --> 00:22:43,279
All right.

274
00:23:35,206 --> 00:23:37,667
There are great meal kits these days.

275
00:23:38,668 --> 00:23:40,419
Before your boyfriend arrives,

276
00:23:40,545 --> 00:23:42,713
ditch the packaging
to destroy the evidence.

277
00:23:43,923 --> 00:23:47,677
Put the chopped scallions
and minced garlic into containers,

278
00:23:47,802 --> 00:23:49,470
and pretend they're yours.

279
00:23:49,595 --> 00:23:53,099
Six out of ten will buy it,
and four will just play along.

280
00:23:54,517 --> 00:23:56,769
Try to date one of the six who'd buy it.

281
00:23:57,728 --> 00:23:59,397
Dense people should date each other.

282
00:24:01,399 --> 00:24:02,358
I don't want to.

283
00:24:03,276 --> 00:24:05,278
I'm going to date you.

284
00:24:09,115 --> 00:24:11,033
You're starting to fall for me, right?

285
00:24:11,159 --> 00:24:13,119
Then keep falling for me.

286
00:24:14,245 --> 00:24:16,664
I'll make you really, really happy.

287
00:24:17,957 --> 00:24:19,542
I'm confident I can.

288
00:24:23,296 --> 00:24:24,589
No.

289
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:26,883
You'll be jobless soon.

290
00:24:27,550 --> 00:24:30,219
I don't like women with no future.
It's not attractive.

291
00:24:33,264 --> 00:24:34,891
My resume can get me anywhere.

292
00:24:36,350 --> 00:24:38,311
Once I clear my name at the hearing,

293
00:24:38,436 --> 00:24:39,729
I'll submit my resignation.

294
00:24:39,854 --> 00:24:42,607
-In two months--
-Think this won't happen elsewhere?

295
00:24:44,609 --> 00:24:46,611
Are you going to run away then, too?

296
00:24:47,570 --> 00:24:48,404
Am I wrong?

297
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:50,740
You were right but dismissed,

298
00:24:51,574 --> 00:24:53,534
while those in the wrong stand proud.

299
00:24:54,619 --> 00:24:55,995
And yet the world

300
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:59,832
keeps turning as if nothing happened,
leaving you furious.

301
00:24:59,957 --> 00:25:01,709
That's why you're running away.

302
00:25:07,924 --> 00:25:09,217
Why can't I?

303
00:25:10,801 --> 00:25:12,220
If I accept

304
00:25:12,803 --> 00:25:15,181
what is wrong, then I'm just like them.

305
00:25:16,140 --> 00:25:19,977
That's not who I want to be.
I refuse to live like that.

306
00:25:22,271 --> 00:25:23,481
Then don't.

307
00:25:24,565 --> 00:25:25,524
But if you refuse,

308
00:25:27,026 --> 00:25:29,028
you won't even make it 100 meters.

309
00:25:29,904 --> 00:25:33,032
The life ahead of you
is 5,000 kilometers long.

310
00:25:34,367 --> 00:25:36,285
Yet with those noble convictions,

311
00:25:36,410 --> 00:25:38,120
values, and principles,

312
00:25:39,497 --> 00:25:41,958
you won't make it 100 meters
keeping them all intact.

313
00:25:42,792 --> 00:25:44,710
I'm not telling you to break them.

314
00:25:47,088 --> 00:25:49,215
If people like you disappear,

315
00:25:50,341 --> 00:25:52,260
it's even better for those people.

316
00:25:52,385 --> 00:25:53,386
Isn't that so unfair?

317
00:25:56,430 --> 00:25:58,224
I felt so, so wronged.

318
00:25:59,850 --> 00:26:01,519
I was so, so furious.

319
00:26:02,603 --> 00:26:03,437
So…

320
00:26:05,189 --> 00:26:07,817
instead of breaking them,
I let them get chipped away.

321
00:26:08,943 --> 00:26:13,072
I told myself,
"I can just cut off some parts."

322
00:26:14,740 --> 00:26:17,285
That's the compromise I made with myself.

323
00:26:20,538 --> 00:26:21,539
So…

324
00:26:23,082 --> 00:26:24,792
just cut off some parts.

325
00:26:27,211 --> 00:26:29,922
If you want to protect
your convictions and values,

326
00:26:32,049 --> 00:26:35,344
let them get chipped away
and just cut parts of them.

327
00:26:53,696 --> 00:26:55,031
Head home now.

328
00:26:55,156 --> 00:26:56,324
I don't want to.

329
00:26:57,283 --> 00:26:58,117
One more lap.

330
00:26:58,242 --> 00:27:01,078
We've done ten laps. My legs hurt.

331
00:27:01,203 --> 00:27:04,206
We barely have any time left.
You can't even do that for me?

332
00:27:04,332 --> 00:27:05,624
Han Tae-seung.

333
00:27:15,926 --> 00:27:19,305
You hugged that Director Tak
or whatever he's called.

334
00:27:20,306 --> 00:27:21,265
Let me have this.

335
00:27:24,268 --> 00:27:25,186
You know what?

336
00:27:26,312 --> 00:27:27,438
Lee Mi-do.

337
00:27:28,439 --> 00:27:30,399
You're a better person than I thought.

338
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:34,278
That's why

339
00:27:34,945 --> 00:27:36,614
I think I can let you go.

340
00:27:38,324 --> 00:27:39,784
I think I have to.

341
00:27:44,372 --> 00:27:45,831
I'm going to get over you.

342
00:27:46,540 --> 00:27:49,168
I really, truly will.

343
00:27:50,211 --> 00:27:51,545
Just watch me.

344
00:27:54,590 --> 00:27:56,300
I will get over you.

345
00:28:09,605 --> 00:28:11,941
Who the hell are you, you bastard? Huh?

346
00:28:12,983 --> 00:28:14,235
Mi-do, are you crazy?

347
00:28:14,360 --> 00:28:16,529
Who is this bastard?

348
00:28:19,407 --> 00:28:21,742
Are you cheating with him?

349
00:28:21,867 --> 00:28:23,494
On Namgung Ho?

350
00:28:23,619 --> 00:28:24,995
Have you lost your mind?

351
00:28:25,121 --> 00:28:27,415
Namgung Ho is seeing someone else too.

352
00:28:27,540 --> 00:28:30,209
-Han Tae-seung.
-That bastard Namgung Ho

353
00:28:30,334 --> 00:28:32,378
is seeing someone else too.

354
00:28:40,594 --> 00:28:41,429
HONDURAS KARAOKE

355
00:28:41,554 --> 00:28:43,305
I'll go with you starting this weekend.

356
00:28:44,014 --> 00:28:45,850
Don't you dare go alone.

357
00:28:47,560 --> 00:28:48,727
Weren't you mad at me?

358
00:28:48,853 --> 00:28:50,980
Don't be so dense.

359
00:28:52,815 --> 00:28:54,900
I'm not mad. I'm just upset.

360
00:28:57,278 --> 00:28:59,155
How many meters deep are you?

361
00:29:02,032 --> 00:29:03,200
How far down…

362
00:29:05,119 --> 00:29:06,579
are you right now?

363
00:29:12,460 --> 00:29:15,838
Yeong-do! What are you doing?
Are you crazy?

364
00:29:17,339 --> 00:29:20,342
It's not true, right? Tell me it isn't.

365
00:29:27,099 --> 00:29:28,225
Let's talk outside.

366
00:29:28,350 --> 00:29:31,812
Why? Worried it will shock this kid?

367
00:29:34,190 --> 00:29:36,108
It's about Sang-su.
Just a misunderstanding.

368
00:29:36,233 --> 00:29:37,651
He broke up with Lee Mi-do.

369
00:29:39,111 --> 00:29:40,029
Yeong-do.

370
00:29:40,154 --> 00:29:43,532
Lee Mi-do is seeing that lawyer punk
from his army days,

371
00:29:43,657 --> 00:29:45,367
and he's dating a junior at work.

372
00:29:45,493 --> 00:29:46,327
That's a lie.

373
00:29:47,328 --> 00:29:48,454
It's not true, right?

374
00:29:48,579 --> 00:29:50,915
He's got it all wrong, right?

375
00:29:52,416 --> 00:29:54,251
Lee Mi-do has always been crazy.

376
00:29:54,376 --> 00:29:56,504
She's never been in her right mind.

377
00:29:56,629 --> 00:29:59,632
So you should've held onto her!

378
00:29:59,757 --> 00:30:03,302
Sure, she probably messed up first.

379
00:30:03,427 --> 00:30:06,722
She caused trouble first, obviously!

380
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:09,642
Still, you had no right to do this.

381
00:30:09,767 --> 00:30:13,479
No matter what she did, you had no right.

382
00:30:13,604 --> 00:30:15,731
Who caused my dad to…

383
00:30:26,116 --> 00:30:27,284
I didn't mean that.

384
00:30:29,453 --> 00:30:30,913
Wasn't it enough?

385
00:30:34,959 --> 00:30:37,127
Was everything I did still not enough?

386
00:30:42,967 --> 00:30:44,843
I thought I did my best…

387
00:30:47,972 --> 00:30:51,183
to repay the price of your dad's life.

388
00:30:52,476 --> 00:30:53,561
Hey, Namgung.

389
00:30:57,856 --> 00:30:59,275
I'm asking you.

390
00:31:01,026 --> 00:31:01,986
Answer me.

391
00:31:06,407 --> 00:31:07,783
Wasn't it enough?

392
00:31:15,499 --> 00:31:17,835
I cleaned up after your family members,

393
00:31:19,670 --> 00:31:22,172
every day out of guilt.

394
00:31:24,091 --> 00:31:25,634
I gave everything I had…

395
00:31:27,303 --> 00:31:30,764
to pay back the price of his life.

396
00:31:33,100 --> 00:31:34,351
You know what?

397
00:31:36,520 --> 00:31:38,939
Every single day was hell for me.

398
00:31:40,608 --> 00:31:42,526
Ever since I survived that day,

399
00:31:43,944 --> 00:31:45,738
there's not been a single moment…

400
00:31:46,739 --> 00:31:48,824
truly, not a single moment,

401
00:31:49,533 --> 00:31:51,368
when I've been happy.

402
00:31:52,036 --> 00:31:52,995
You know that?

403
00:32:05,799 --> 00:32:07,801
Dad died because of me.

404
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:18,604
That day,

405
00:32:19,730 --> 00:32:21,815
Dad didn't want to go in the water.

406
00:32:23,817 --> 00:32:25,277
But I threw a fit,

407
00:32:26,820 --> 00:32:28,322
so he went to save him.

408
00:32:30,824 --> 00:32:32,368
It wasn't because of Namgung.

409
00:32:33,827 --> 00:32:35,037
It was because of me.

410
00:32:37,790 --> 00:32:39,708
Dad died because of me.

411
00:32:57,059 --> 00:32:58,435
Namgung, I'm sorry.

412
00:33:00,979 --> 00:33:02,648
I was such a coward.

413
00:33:04,191 --> 00:33:05,651
I hid behind you.

414
00:33:07,945 --> 00:33:09,488
For far too long,

415
00:33:10,948 --> 00:33:12,408
I hid behind you.

416
00:33:16,370 --> 00:33:17,371
I'm sorry.

417
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:23,585
I'm so, so sorry.

418
00:33:51,780 --> 00:33:53,907
Namgung won't forgive me, will he?

419
00:33:54,867 --> 00:33:56,201
He'll never see me again.

420
00:33:58,704 --> 00:34:00,122
Don't be ridiculous.

421
00:34:06,628 --> 00:34:07,838
Wait.

422
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:10,883
Why are you sitting over there?

423
00:34:11,008 --> 00:34:12,718
Wanna get punched some more?

424
00:34:14,428 --> 00:34:15,262
Yes.

425
00:34:16,638 --> 00:34:19,349
My injuries won't last four weeks,
so I can't sue.

426
00:34:22,853 --> 00:34:23,854
Punch me some more.

427
00:34:25,022 --> 00:34:28,275
That's the only way
I'll come to my senses.

428
00:34:56,720 --> 00:34:59,973
Your dad was named Model Firefighter
three times.

429
00:35:02,768 --> 00:35:05,938
Believing he came to save me
just because you begged…

430
00:35:08,065 --> 00:35:10,108
is a huge insult to your dad.

431
00:35:12,236 --> 00:35:14,154
And what I said to Yeong-do earlier…

432
00:35:15,197 --> 00:35:16,907
I just got so mad.

433
00:35:20,494 --> 00:35:22,412
I said it without thinking.

434
00:35:25,374 --> 00:35:27,167
Yeah, it's true I felt guilty.

435
00:35:28,919 --> 00:35:30,504
And indebted, too. But…

436
00:35:36,343 --> 00:35:37,678
But I…

437
00:35:41,598 --> 00:35:42,724
I really…

438
00:35:45,686 --> 00:35:47,312
Mi-do, I really did…

439
00:36:09,418 --> 00:36:10,460
I know.

440
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:13,547
You were happy, right?

441
00:36:17,634 --> 00:36:23,015
Being able to do something for my family
made you happy, right?

442
00:36:26,476 --> 00:36:28,061
How could I not know that?

443
00:36:29,229 --> 00:36:31,607
Of course I know, you dummy.

444
00:36:35,652 --> 00:36:38,864
Stop living like that.
People will walk all over you.

445
00:36:46,455 --> 00:36:49,333
I'm happy.

446
00:36:51,668 --> 00:36:53,921
I was happy I could do something for you.

447
00:36:54,838 --> 00:36:56,924
So I never felt tired running.

448
00:36:57,674 --> 00:36:59,301
I was so, so happy.

449
00:37:02,763 --> 00:37:06,183
Mi-do, even I think I'm pretty weird.

450
00:37:08,101 --> 00:37:10,979
Helping someone I care about
gives me strength.

451
00:37:12,230 --> 00:37:14,399
I don't care
if it means losing everything.

452
00:37:14,524 --> 00:37:15,817
It just makes me happy.

453
00:37:23,408 --> 00:37:25,535
You'll just be called a pushover

454
00:37:26,870 --> 00:37:27,829
and taken advantage of.

455
00:37:27,955 --> 00:37:29,498
It's not being taken advantage of.

456
00:37:30,958 --> 00:37:35,420
It makes me really, truly happy.

457
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:37,714
You dummy.

458
00:37:57,943 --> 00:37:59,194
Namgung.

459
00:38:01,154 --> 00:38:03,198
That's just who you are.

460
00:38:04,950 --> 00:38:07,202
Someone who knows the joy of giving.

461
00:38:09,871 --> 00:38:11,581
And who's happy because of it.

462
00:38:12,791 --> 00:38:17,129
People who don't understand
call that having low self-esteem.

463
00:38:19,006 --> 00:38:21,800
They say you just want to be loved.

464
00:38:26,972 --> 00:38:28,265
But that's not it.

465
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:39,276
You have more love than anyone.

466
00:38:43,530 --> 00:38:49,786
Giving your love makes you truly happy
because you have so much of it.

467
00:38:59,254 --> 00:39:02,674
A pushover isn't someone who is stupid
or easy to manipulate.

468
00:39:04,551 --> 00:39:06,470
They're someone with a lot to give.

469
00:39:08,930 --> 00:39:12,559
That's why you can give to others.
Because you have so much.

470
00:39:13,643 --> 00:39:15,479
And because you can fill up again,

471
00:39:16,605 --> 00:39:20,984
you can gladly give away
everything you have.

472
00:39:24,362 --> 00:39:25,530
Right?

473
00:39:33,080 --> 00:39:35,415
You're a happy pushover.

474
00:39:39,461 --> 00:39:40,837
Aren't you?

475
00:39:52,766 --> 00:39:53,975
Mi-do.

476
00:39:55,018 --> 00:39:56,520
Yeah?

477
00:39:58,647 --> 00:40:00,565
Don't grow up.

478
00:40:06,404 --> 00:40:08,573
Don't grow up, Mi-do.

479
00:40:12,077 --> 00:40:13,829
Don't grow up.

480
00:40:28,885 --> 00:40:29,719
QUEENS SALON

481
00:40:29,845 --> 00:40:32,430
So what's Mi-do been doing lately?

482
00:40:32,556 --> 00:40:33,431
Don't.

483
00:40:34,558 --> 00:40:36,601
She's marrying Namgung soon, right?

484
00:40:36,726 --> 00:40:39,521
A woman just needs to marry well.

485
00:40:39,646 --> 00:40:40,772
Right.

486
00:40:41,773 --> 00:40:44,734
-Just quiet down and read your magazine.
-Okay.

487
00:41:00,208 --> 00:41:01,835
Ms. Ma, want to head to Daehak-ro?

488
00:41:06,882 --> 00:41:08,800
Let's sell these and get some good food.

489
00:41:08,925 --> 00:41:09,926
Deal?

490
00:41:25,483 --> 00:41:26,568
What about work?

491
00:41:27,736 --> 00:41:29,279
Took a half-day.

492
00:41:30,822 --> 00:41:34,117
The weather was just so nice
on my way to work this morning.

493
00:41:34,868 --> 00:41:37,746
So I thought of you and played hooky.

494
00:41:37,871 --> 00:41:39,289
Just like me.

495
00:41:40,332 --> 00:41:43,710
Too nice a day
to just spend it rolling perms.

496
00:41:43,835 --> 00:41:45,545
Liar.

497
00:41:54,387 --> 00:41:56,014
You know everything, don't you?

498
00:41:59,893 --> 00:42:03,647
So you won't even try?

499
00:42:10,362 --> 00:42:12,322
Trying isn't the hard part.

500
00:42:13,949 --> 00:42:15,700
I just feel so terribly sorry.

501
00:42:17,744 --> 00:42:19,746
I'm so sorry…

502
00:42:22,165 --> 00:42:23,917
that I can't do this.

503
00:42:27,712 --> 00:42:28,964
I'm sorry.

504
00:42:32,592 --> 00:42:33,551
Ho.

505
00:42:34,719 --> 00:42:37,305
Remember what I told you before?

506
00:42:38,306 --> 00:42:40,934
Yeong-do is the soft one.

507
00:42:41,059 --> 00:42:42,727
Wan-do is the mean one.

508
00:42:43,853 --> 00:42:45,855
Mi-do is the kind one.

509
00:42:47,691 --> 00:42:50,151
What kind of guy do you think you are?

510
00:42:57,075 --> 00:42:58,368
The…

511
00:42:59,911 --> 00:43:01,121
best-looking one?

512
00:43:01,788 --> 00:43:03,248
Don't flatter yourself.

513
00:43:12,007 --> 00:43:13,967
The most pathetic one?

514
00:43:16,177 --> 00:43:17,262
The heartbreaking one?

515
00:43:18,513 --> 00:43:19,764
No?

516
00:43:21,349 --> 00:43:22,183
I know.

517
00:43:23,560 --> 00:43:24,936
The one you hate most.

518
00:43:25,603 --> 00:43:27,022
The one you hate the most

519
00:43:27,147 --> 00:43:29,733
but feel too sorry for to ever truly hate.

520
00:43:29,858 --> 00:43:30,775
Right?

521
00:43:32,569 --> 00:43:33,611
No.

522
00:43:36,406 --> 00:43:37,699
The precious one.

523
00:43:42,579 --> 00:43:44,205
The one I love most.

524
00:43:48,585 --> 00:43:50,670
Back then,

525
00:43:52,047 --> 00:43:54,090
when you were so young,

526
00:43:55,216 --> 00:43:59,220
I said such awful things to you,
things I could barely bring myself to say,

527
00:43:59,346 --> 00:44:01,473
and it weighed on my mind forever.

528
00:44:03,266 --> 00:44:05,393
I was furious.

529
00:44:06,227 --> 00:44:09,564
I thought, "Who was this kid
who killed my husband,

530
00:44:09,689 --> 00:44:12,442
to stay stuck in my heart like a thorn?"

531
00:44:13,026 --> 00:44:14,402
No matter how I looked at it,

532
00:44:14,527 --> 00:44:17,238
I thought I had
every right to be like that.

533
00:44:18,031 --> 00:44:19,908
No matter how young you were,

534
00:44:20,033 --> 00:44:23,328
I thought I had the right
to take it all out on you.

535
00:44:27,499 --> 00:44:29,709
How else was I supposed to survive?

536
00:44:31,336 --> 00:44:35,006
Without someone to tear into,
how was I supposed to survive?

537
00:44:37,258 --> 00:44:39,594
That's why I went to see you.

538
00:44:40,887 --> 00:44:43,348
You kept crossing my mind,

539
00:44:43,473 --> 00:44:46,601
not as a thorn,

540
00:44:46,726 --> 00:44:48,561
and not out of guilt.

541
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:51,481
I wanted to believe I just hated you.

542
00:44:53,066 --> 00:44:55,360
I figured if I saw your face,

543
00:44:55,485 --> 00:44:57,904
I might be able to hate you more.

544
00:45:02,283 --> 00:45:04,619
-Thank you.
-Enjoy your food.

545
00:45:06,996 --> 00:45:10,667
-Enjoy.
-It's spicy. Would you like a little?

546
00:45:13,169 --> 00:45:14,504
Enjoy your food.

547
00:45:15,171 --> 00:45:17,298
Green light, red light!

548
00:45:17,424 --> 00:45:19,300
Green light, red light!

549
00:45:19,426 --> 00:45:21,010
Green light…

550
00:45:21,136 --> 00:45:22,429
-Namgung!
-You're it!

551
00:45:22,554 --> 00:45:25,807
-You're it!
-You're it!

552
00:45:25,932 --> 00:45:27,517
-You're it!
-Freeze!

553
00:45:28,476 --> 00:45:30,728
-Come here.
-Unfreeze me.

554
00:45:41,906 --> 00:45:45,493
But you were just so lovely.

555
00:45:46,286 --> 00:45:48,830
I went to find a reason to hate you,

556
00:45:48,955 --> 00:45:51,458
but all I saw was how lovely you were.

557
00:45:55,336 --> 00:45:57,088
So I brought you home.

558
00:46:01,885 --> 00:46:03,261
Because you were lovely.

559
00:46:05,013 --> 00:46:08,892
Too lovely to leave in a place like that.

560
00:46:16,024 --> 00:46:17,066
Ho.

561
00:46:18,318 --> 00:46:19,319
Out of everyone,

562
00:46:19,903 --> 00:46:23,740
I have the most reason to hate you.

563
00:46:25,200 --> 00:46:28,703
So if you were that lovely to me,

564
00:46:29,579 --> 00:46:32,999
then you really are a lovely person.

565
00:46:37,712 --> 00:46:40,465
You must never forget that.

566
00:46:45,303 --> 00:46:46,721
Even if,

567
00:46:47,889 --> 00:46:49,766
even if by some rare chance,

568
00:46:49,891 --> 00:46:51,684
you break up with Mi-do

569
00:46:53,603 --> 00:46:56,481
and you end up all alone again,

570
00:46:58,149 --> 00:46:59,567
as long as you remember this,

571
00:47:00,235 --> 00:47:02,779
you can still live a good life.

572
00:47:04,864 --> 00:47:08,368
That will get you through
the rest of your life.

573
00:47:13,456 --> 00:47:14,624
Mi-do

574
00:47:15,333 --> 00:47:16,543
will be fine.

575
00:47:18,086 --> 00:47:22,215
She's much stronger than you think.

576
00:47:24,259 --> 00:47:27,178
I was too busy scraping by
to raise her like that,

577
00:47:29,055 --> 00:47:31,057
but you raised her that way.

578
00:47:36,020 --> 00:47:38,898
You did such a wonderful job.

579
00:48:00,503 --> 00:48:01,588
Is the rumor true?

580
00:48:02,755 --> 00:48:03,881
It isn't, right?

581
00:48:04,007 --> 00:48:05,383
Please tell me it isn't.

582
00:48:09,846 --> 00:48:10,805
It's true.

583
00:48:11,598 --> 00:48:14,267
I've been transferred
to the Tongyeong factory.

584
00:48:14,392 --> 00:48:17,520
You can probably stay at headquarters.

585
00:48:17,645 --> 00:48:19,355
But I've had previous incidents…

586
00:48:19,480 --> 00:48:21,399
That's not what I'm asking.

587
00:48:24,277 --> 00:48:25,695
Did you really restore it?

588
00:48:25,820 --> 00:48:27,447
Did you restore the footage?

589
00:48:29,490 --> 00:48:31,909
Yeah, Namgung did.

590
00:48:33,036 --> 00:48:34,704
He's a real tough cookie.

591
00:48:35,872 --> 00:48:38,541
That's why he took it
to Executive Director Yoon.

592
00:48:43,129 --> 00:48:44,505
It was Namgung's call.

593
00:48:46,174 --> 00:48:50,094
It's thanks to him
that I at least got sent to Tongyeong,

594
00:48:50,762 --> 00:48:52,430
and you get to stay at headquarters.

595
00:48:58,394 --> 00:49:00,355
You've never let me down until now.

596
00:49:03,149 --> 00:49:04,484
You gave that footage…

597
00:49:06,611 --> 00:49:08,446
knowing he could do it, didn't you?

598
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:09,405
Or rather,

599
00:49:10,657 --> 00:49:12,492
so he wouldn't expose it

600
00:49:13,201 --> 00:49:16,037
and instead cut a deal
with Executive Director Yoon, right?

601
00:49:17,747 --> 00:49:20,875
You did it knowing
how he'd been chipped away at.

602
00:49:21,584 --> 00:49:23,836
How could you do that?

603
00:49:25,213 --> 00:49:27,173
To him, of all people!

604
00:49:28,716 --> 00:49:30,551
How could you do this?

605
00:49:33,346 --> 00:49:37,308
After everything he suffered…

606
00:49:38,101 --> 00:49:41,688
Because I've been chipped away
down to nothing.

607
00:49:41,813 --> 00:49:43,272
I had nothing left to lose.

608
00:49:46,025 --> 00:49:47,318
I'm sorry.

609
00:49:58,204 --> 00:49:59,414
For the Taegye-ri case,

610
00:50:00,832 --> 00:50:02,625
find another lawyer.

611
00:50:02,750 --> 00:50:03,960
Han Tae-seung won't take it.

612
00:50:12,218 --> 00:50:16,264
That's not for you to decide,
Director Lee Mi-do.

613
00:50:18,099 --> 00:50:19,726
Do you know why he likes me?

614
00:50:21,602 --> 00:50:23,479
Because I'm a crazy bitch.

615
00:50:27,859 --> 00:50:29,485
Just out of curiosity,

616
00:50:30,069 --> 00:50:33,656
you're not playing that Song Hae-na card
to threaten me, are you?

617
00:50:33,781 --> 00:50:35,783
I'd really be disappointed then.

618
00:50:35,908 --> 00:50:36,826
That's no fun.

619
00:50:41,831 --> 00:50:44,333
Besides Park Pil-du,
the leader of the Jaeseon Party,

620
00:50:45,126 --> 00:50:47,920
there are plenty of takers
for the Song Hae-na card.

621
00:50:49,714 --> 00:50:52,592
You and your father-in-law
have so many enemies.

622
00:50:56,637 --> 00:50:58,431
I made myself clear.

623
00:50:58,556 --> 00:51:01,476
Don't give the Taegye-ri case
to Han Tae-seung.

624
00:51:03,352 --> 00:51:05,229
Don't give him any shady cases.

625
00:51:05,354 --> 00:51:06,481
Actually,

626
00:51:07,523 --> 00:51:10,485
stop messing with him. Don't come around.

627
00:51:18,326 --> 00:51:19,619
I'm not going to him.

628
00:51:22,163 --> 00:51:23,372
He comes to me.

629
00:51:47,313 --> 00:51:49,398
Do you have any idea what you did?

630
00:51:50,525 --> 00:51:53,444
I threatened Seo Ju-hyeok
and got caught by you.

631
00:51:53,569 --> 00:51:54,403
So I'm pissed.

632
00:51:54,529 --> 00:51:59,408
You think Seo Ju-hyeok is a pushover
just because you can push me around?

633
00:52:00,618 --> 00:52:01,869
I let you off easy

634
00:52:01,994 --> 00:52:04,539
on the settlement agreement
because I liked you.

635
00:52:04,664 --> 00:52:06,749
If I'd handled that like my other cases,

636
00:52:06,874 --> 00:52:08,084
you wouldn't be here.

637
00:52:10,211 --> 00:52:11,254
Han Tae-seung.

638
00:52:11,379 --> 00:52:14,340
-You don't have time to relax--
-Want to go get udon?

639
00:52:16,509 --> 00:52:17,802
Let's go get udon.

640
00:52:28,187 --> 00:52:29,021
JEONGDAM UDON

641
00:52:29,146 --> 00:52:32,859
I promised to find out
why you wander around Myeong-dong.

642
00:52:34,652 --> 00:52:35,528
Seriously.

643
00:52:37,738 --> 00:52:39,574
That's quite a parting gift.

644
00:52:41,909 --> 00:52:43,494
How long have you known?

645
00:52:51,794 --> 00:52:53,045
I said, how long?

646
00:52:53,170 --> 00:52:54,422
Known about what?

647
00:52:54,547 --> 00:52:57,091
That this udon is the reason
you roamed Myeong-dong?

648
00:52:58,843 --> 00:53:00,887
Or that this udon shop turns out to be

649
00:53:01,012 --> 00:53:03,806
full of memories
you made with Seo Ju-hyeok?

650
00:53:08,060 --> 00:53:10,104
That you love Seo Ju-hyeok so much?

651
00:53:12,648 --> 00:53:13,566
Are you crazy?

652
00:53:14,317 --> 00:53:15,651
I'm crazy about women!

653
00:53:17,194 --> 00:53:20,531
I knew from the day
I called you Seo Ju-hyeok's lapdog.

654
00:53:22,617 --> 00:53:25,995
That you really care about Seo Ju-hyeok.

655
00:53:29,832 --> 00:53:31,876
You looked really sad back then.

656
00:53:35,212 --> 00:53:38,883
You handled the Taegye-ri matter
for his sake, right?

657
00:53:39,759 --> 00:53:42,345
When his father-in-law
pressured Seo Ju-hyeok,

658
00:53:43,054 --> 00:53:46,015
you looked into it to help him.

659
00:53:47,934 --> 00:53:49,727
What? That's not true.

660
00:53:52,021 --> 00:53:53,439
I said it's not.

661
00:53:53,564 --> 00:53:54,815
I told you.

662
00:53:56,525 --> 00:53:59,236
I know you better than you think.

663
00:54:02,531 --> 00:54:04,617
Your Honor.

664
00:54:04,742 --> 00:54:06,702
The defendant, Han Tae-seung,

665
00:54:06,827 --> 00:54:10,581
may indeed have killed the victim.

666
00:54:16,128 --> 00:54:19,757
Yet the reason I defended him
and argued for his innocence

667
00:54:20,341 --> 00:54:21,884
is that Han Tae-seung

668
00:54:23,260 --> 00:54:25,805
so earnestly told me

669
00:54:26,597 --> 00:54:27,765
he was not the killer.

670
00:54:27,890 --> 00:54:32,395
I respectfully ask Your Honor
to give this 16-year-old boy

671
00:54:32,520 --> 00:54:36,273
the strength to live on
so that he is no longer alone.

672
00:54:40,736 --> 00:54:42,488
You must miss him so much.

673
00:54:43,447 --> 00:54:45,324
The Seo Ju-hyeok from back then.

674
00:54:48,077 --> 00:54:49,495
But Han Tae-seung.

675
00:54:51,414 --> 00:54:55,126
You can never see that Seo Ju-hyeok again.

676
00:54:58,379 --> 00:54:59,213
Wait.

677
00:55:00,548 --> 00:55:02,133
There's one way.

678
00:55:03,551 --> 00:55:04,802
Want me to tell you?

679
00:55:16,981 --> 00:55:18,774
You just have to become him.

680
00:55:22,236 --> 00:55:23,612
The Seo Ju-hyeok back then.

681
00:55:23,738 --> 00:55:26,073
Seo Ju-hyeok, the good lawyer.

682
00:55:26,782 --> 00:55:28,159
You can be him.

683
00:55:30,119 --> 00:55:32,621
You were probably a good kid.

684
00:55:36,083 --> 00:55:37,168
Really.

685
00:55:38,753 --> 00:55:41,005
A really good kid.

686
00:56:09,408 --> 00:56:10,659
Why did you do it?

687
00:56:12,244 --> 00:56:14,997
You didn't have to do anything.

688
00:56:18,167 --> 00:56:19,335
Why go that far…

689
00:56:19,460 --> 00:56:21,462
I wanted you to hang on.

690
00:56:23,923 --> 00:56:25,466
At least HQ is better.

691
00:56:26,592 --> 00:56:28,385
There's at least hope there.

692
00:56:29,595 --> 00:56:32,181
Hang in there. Grit your teeth.

693
00:56:34,934 --> 00:56:38,187
This is the first and last time
I let myself be chipped away for you.

694
00:56:40,481 --> 00:56:42,483
So whenever you want to run away,

695
00:56:42,608 --> 00:56:45,236
remember how I got chipped away for you,

696
00:56:46,612 --> 00:56:49,907
and how painful it was for me and hang on.

697
00:56:51,659 --> 00:56:54,370
In life, there are things
you'd never do for yourself,

698
00:56:56,080 --> 00:56:59,708
but strangely, you can endure them
for someone else.

699
00:57:07,299 --> 00:57:10,094
My biological father was total trash.

700
00:57:12,012 --> 00:57:14,223
He was a famous gangster in Busan,

701
00:57:15,850 --> 00:57:18,477
and dozens of people
were left disabled because of him.

702
00:57:21,188 --> 00:57:24,692
I hated having his genes so much.

703
00:57:25,359 --> 00:57:26,485
I was scared.

704
00:57:28,028 --> 00:57:28,988
But…

705
00:57:30,865 --> 00:57:33,701
they say I'm good at drawing
because I take after him.

706
00:57:37,288 --> 00:57:40,166
As soon as I found that out,
I quit drawing.

707
00:57:42,585 --> 00:57:45,671
Because I hated having
his genes inside me so much.

708
00:57:48,382 --> 00:57:52,469
The talent that made me feel
that the world was fair

709
00:57:53,846 --> 00:57:56,473
came from him,
and it disgusted me so much.

710
00:58:03,480 --> 00:58:06,483
This is my secret and shame
that not even Lee Mi-do knows.

711
00:58:08,485 --> 00:58:11,697
Park Su-a, I kept my promise,
so you keep yours.

712
00:58:13,115 --> 00:58:14,325
Starting tomorrow,

713
00:58:16,535 --> 00:58:18,913
we're coworkers.
Nothing more, nothing less.

714
00:59:00,829 --> 00:59:02,289
You're wrong.

715
00:59:03,290 --> 00:59:04,625
I'm not a good kid.

716
00:59:07,461 --> 00:59:09,922
You know I didn't do it
just for Seo Ju-hyeok.

717
00:59:14,677 --> 00:59:16,720
I'm someone who found it easy.

718
00:59:16,845 --> 00:59:18,764
That's why I could do it.

719
00:59:20,516 --> 00:59:21,558
But…

720
00:59:23,185 --> 00:59:24,478
since you want it,

721
00:59:26,814 --> 00:59:28,857
I'll give it a try.

722
00:59:28,983 --> 00:59:31,902
I'll try with everything I've got.

723
00:59:35,197 --> 00:59:36,365
So please…

724
00:59:40,953 --> 00:59:42,663
don't leave me.

725
00:59:44,081 --> 00:59:45,124
I'll be good.

726
00:59:47,668 --> 00:59:48,961
Don't leave me.

727
01:00:10,482 --> 01:00:11,775
You…

728
01:00:13,152 --> 01:00:15,195
You've never held me before.

729
01:00:19,825 --> 01:00:22,119
How can you hold me while leaving me?

730
01:00:33,797 --> 01:00:35,132
If you do this,

731
01:00:37,092 --> 01:00:38,844
how am I supposed to forget you?

732
01:00:40,387 --> 01:00:42,681
I'm the one
who's really not a good person.

733
01:00:45,893 --> 01:00:48,604
I think this is how I can forget you.

734
01:00:50,731 --> 01:00:52,483
I'll feel less guilty.

735
01:00:56,362 --> 01:00:57,363
I'm sorry.

736
01:01:27,476 --> 01:01:28,602
You're a coward.

737
01:01:30,354 --> 01:01:32,064
I had such high hopes.

738
01:01:33,565 --> 01:01:36,068
If I knew a secret Ms. Lee didn't,

739
01:01:36,777 --> 01:01:38,821
I was ready to settle for that.

740
01:01:42,282 --> 01:01:44,410
You said to let myself get chipped away?

741
01:01:45,494 --> 01:01:46,620
Fine.

742
01:01:47,621 --> 01:01:48,705
I will.

743
01:01:51,083 --> 01:01:52,167
I'll be a coward.

744
01:01:53,252 --> 01:01:55,045
I won't keep that promise.

745
01:01:55,754 --> 01:01:57,840
Even if you marry Lee Mi-do,

746
01:01:57,965 --> 01:02:00,801
I'll keep loving you
and stay right by your side.

747
01:03:04,656 --> 01:03:05,908
THANK YOU TO LEE SANG-YI
FOR HIS SPECIAL APPEARANCE

748
01:03:06,033 --> 01:03:09,119
Tell me you don't miss Namgung Ho at all.

749
01:03:09,244 --> 01:03:12,623
If you and I had met like ordinary people,

750
01:03:12,748 --> 01:03:14,750
our ending would've been different.

751
01:03:14,875 --> 01:03:17,586
I just broke up with Han Tae-seung
and came straight here.

752
01:03:17,711 --> 01:03:21,215
You're the one who taught me
that life could be this happy.

753
01:03:21,340 --> 01:03:23,634
Why are we such a mess?

754
01:03:23,759 --> 01:03:26,637
What can we do? It's just who we are.

755
01:03:30,474 --> 01:03:32,434
Subtitle Translation by Soya Back
